{"tool_name":"tadbit","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"tadbit","identifiers":["biotools:tadbit","doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1005665"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"TADbit is a complete Python library to deal with all steps to analyze, model and explore 3C-based data.","home_url":"https://github.com/3DGenomes/tadbit","keywords":["Animals","Chromatin","Computational Biology","Drosophila melanogaster","Genome, Insect","Imaging, Three-Dimensional","Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","DNA packaging","Gene regulation","Genomics","Genetics","Transcription Factors","Transcriptome"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"tadbit","home":"http://3dgenomes.github.io/TADbit/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Computational framework to analyze and model 3C-based experiments.","addition_date":"2018-06-25T14:11:47Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T13:48:06.298475Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:tadbit","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"martirenom@cnag.crg.eu","name":"Marc A. Marti-Renom","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://3dgenomes.github.io/TADbit/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Raw sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0848"},"format":[{"term":"FASTQ","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1930"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Nucleic acid folding analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0279"},{"term":"Pathway or network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2497"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2403"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2048"},"format":[{"term":"Graph format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3617"},{"term":"Matrix format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3033"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"TADbit","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1005665","metadata":{"abstract":"The sequence of a genome is insufficient to understand all genomic processes carried out in the cell nucleus. To achieve this, the knowledge of its three-dimensional architecture is necessary. Advances in genomic technologies and the development of new analytical methods, such as Chromosome Conformation Capture (3C) and its derivatives, provide unprecedented insights in the spatial organization of genomes. Here we present TADbit, a computational framework to analyze and model the chromatin fiber in three dimensions. Our package takes as input the sequencing reads of 3C-based experiments and performs the following main tasks: (i) pre-process the reads, (ii) map the reads to a reference genome, (iii) filter and normalize the interaction data, (iv) analyze the resulting interaction matrices, (v) build 3D models of selected genomic domains, and (vi) analyze the resulting models to characterize their structural properties. To illustrate the use of TADbit, we automatically modeled 50 genomic domains from the fly genome revealing differential structural features of the previously defined chromatin colors, establishing a link between the conformation of the genome and the local chromatin composition. TADbit provides three-dimensional models built from 3C-based experiments, which are ready for visualization and for characterizing their relation to gene expression and epigenetic states. TADbit is an open-source Python library available for download from https://github.com/3DGenomes/tadbit.","authors":[{"name":"Bau D."},{"name":"Castillo D."},{"name":"Filion G."},{"name":"Goodstadt M."},{"name":"Marti-Renom M.A."},{"name":"Serra F."}],"citationCount":188,"date":"2017-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS Computational Biology","title":"Automatic analysis and 3D-modelling of Hi-C data using TADbit reveals structural features of the fly 